/* book exam traps: MOST is not arbitrated like CAN. Synchronous streams own fixed byte positions in every frame; only the asynchronous and control channels are shared. | One broken fibre stops the whole MOST ring, not just the next device; this is why the ring break diagnosis exists. | A gateway is not a repeater or a bridge: it translates between different protocols and decides which signals cross, up to OSI layer 7. | Forwarding is not free: the crossing message pays its frame time on both buses plus the gateway's processing, and the slow bus pays its load. | The MOST frame rate equals the audio sample rate (44.1 or 48 kHz), so a stream uses bytes per frame, not bits per second, in the frame budget. */
