/* book Worked example 2: Q: Service 03 on a CAN car returns 43 02 03 01 01 33. A freeze frame for the first code gives PID 05 = 0x7B, PID 0D = 0x3E and PID 04 = 0x59. Decode the codes and the freeze frame.
   1. 43 is the reply to service 03; 02 says two codes follow; the codes are 03 01 and 01 33.
   2. 0x0301: first byte 0000 0011. Top two bits 00 → P; next two bits 00 → first digit 0; low four bits 0011 → 3; second byte 0x01 → digits 0 and 1. Code P0301, misfire in cylinder 1.
   3. 0x0133: first byte 0000 0001 → P, 0, 1; second byte 0x33 → 3 and 3. Code P0133, oxygen sensor slow response, bank 1 sensor 1.
   4. Coolant: A = 0x7B = 123, so 123 − 40 = 83 °C (engine warm).
   5. Vehicle speed: A = 0x3E = 62, so 62 km/h.
   6. Engine load: A = 0x59 = 89, so 89 × 100 ÷ 255 = 34.9 per cent.
   Answer: Codes P0301 (cylinder 1 misfire) and P0133 (slow oxygen sensor, bank 1 sensor 1); the misfire was set with the engine warm at 83 °C, at 62 km/h and about 35 per cent load. */
