/* book exam traps: The P in P0301 means powertrain, not petrol. C is chassis, B body, U network. | A generic scan tool does read P1xxx codes through service 03; what it lacks is the maker's table that says what each one means. | Pins 4 and 5 are grounds and pin 16 is battery positive; CAN is on pins 6 and 14, not 6 and 16. | A freeze frame is stored data from the moment the fault was confirmed, read with service 02; live data is service 01. | Clearing codes with service 04 switches the lamp off but does not repair the fault, and it resets the readiness monitors, so the car fails an inspection that checks them. */
